  "evidence": "Main creator sets state slot and invokes 0xc620160 for available data. This builder creates the arrow/mark controls and 0xc620c30 constructs the pillar using conditional image calls; the latter is also called by deferred function 0xc621218. Arrow registrations use filter 7 and callbacks 0xc620091/0xc620055, which call 0xc621090 in opposite directions. The mark registration uses filter 7 and callback 0xc620015. The pillar helper registers 0xc6209cd. Formatting helper 0xc62166c sets the date; 0xc6217b4 sets the two stated status labels. Both helpers have multiple callers.",
  "scope": "These entries filter individual call sites while main state is active. Pillar calls inside loops can fire repeatedly; a single call may receive more than one image. Date/status helper calls may occur from any of their callers while the main state remains active; they do not identify a specific label object. Scroll-update branches are documented in women-scroll-043.json; formatted status strings are not covered by these entries.",
  "limitations": "Both slots are installation guards, not a cross-thread synchronization mechanism. Deferred callbacks, asynchronous destruction, health data effects, recovery and all device behavior require on-device verification. Avoid recording private health values.",
